From b07160e582276647cbe597f51cc050e2b2b2166c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 03:18:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] b10819 sync: repair six merge defects that stopped the tree
 from building

The R13 base move (b10680 -> b10819) landed 532 commits over 6a1a922d2 with the
protected-win anchors intact, but the tree did not compile. Six resolutions were
incomplete. Each is repaired against the parent that owns the surface, never by
dropping a side.

1. src/llama-context.cpp, src/llama-model.cpp - upstream turned llama_hparams
   n_ff_exp / n_expert_used into per-layer accessors (uint32_t f(uint32_t il = 0)).
   The PowerInfer MoE-pipeline and expert-bundle grafts still read them as fields.
   Called with the il=0 default, which is the exact prior single-value semantics.
   CAVEAT: for a model whose layers differ, a global pipeline sized from layer 0 is
   an under-size; n_expert_used_max() exists for that. Not changed here because it
   would be an unmeasured behaviour change on a path this estate cannot exercise.

2. ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp - the TurboQuant tq_rotate staging branch
   still set prealloc_y_last_decode_vector_staging. Upstream 77f132cb1 (mul_mat_id
   pads K rather than N) replaced that member with prealloc_y_last_k_padded; every
   other site in the file had been converted. The rotate path never K-pads, so it
   sets false, mirroring the quantize_y path.

3. src/models/dflash.cpp - the closing brace of the dsv4_hc_mult block was lost, so
   its early return fell into the generic per-layer loop and the file could not
   parse. Restored from prebump/arifi-main-95c1b6e69-20260906.

4. src/models/qwen35.cpp - upstream added n_kv_max to build_attn_mha; the batched
   MTP call site was not updated. Passes 0, the value every dense caller uses (the
   only non-zero is the top-k sparse path).

5. common/speculative.cpp - collision #10 adopted upstream's per-sequence chunked
   DFlash encoder but dropped the i_batch_beg/i_batch_end setup its loop reads, and
   left the fork's older flat encode path dangling after the loop, referencing
   offset/n_chunk/features_buf that no longer exist there. Upstream's setup block is
   restored and the dangling path removed - upstream's fused decode does the encode
   and injection the old path did by hand. The fork's f16 massive-activation
   sanitize is NOT dropped: it is re-grafted onto upstream's chunked buffer, inside
   the loop, before the decode. llama_synchronize is kept per sequence.

Loss control for the whole set: a brace-balance scan over all 226 code files the bump
touched, comparing each file against BOTH parents, reports no file whose balance
matches neither - defect 3 was the only one of its class.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Measured-effect: build FAIL at 6/305 -> RC=0 with all five targets linked (llama-cli, llama-server, llama-quantize, test-backend-ops, test-quantize-fns); runtime effect of the speculative.cpp union is measured by the F-141 content gate and the served DFlash2 arm, not by this build.
Lane: lane-209
